<title>USA: BOXING-JOHNSON RETAINS IBF FLYWEIGHT TITLE.</title>
<headline>BOXING-JOHNSON RETAINS IBF FLYWEIGHT TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>UNCASVILLE, Connecticut 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Boxing Federation flyweight champion Mark Johnson knocked out fellow-American Cecilio Espino in the second round on Sunday to retain his title.</p>
<p>Johnson, who made the third defence of his title, won his 31st consecutive bout and now has a record of 32-1.</p>
<p>Espino fell to 33-6-1.</p>
